      <header><p class="eyebrow">Case study · 2017—2024</p><h1>Rocketeers</h1><p class="lede">Building and operating a cross-border digital marketplace business from the ground up.</p></header>
      <section class="metrics" aria-label="Rocketeers at a glance"><div><strong>23,000</strong><span>items sold</span></div><div><strong>10,000+</strong><span>customer transactions</span></div><div><strong>5,000+</strong><span>customers served</span></div><div><strong>20+</strong><span>countries reached</span></div></section>
      <section class="story"><p class="eyebrow">The work</p><h2>A business where every operating detail mattered.</h2><p>Rocketeers was a digital marketplace business I founded and ran for seven years. It required hands-on ownership across sourcing, listings, pricing, inventory, customer service, returns, disputes, and seller performance.</p><p>Rather than treating marketplace work as a sequence of isolated tasks, I built and refined operating routines that connected customer experience with commercial decisions and platform health.</p></section>
      <section class="columns"><article><p class="eyebrow">Operations</p><h2>From listing to resolution.</h2><ul><li>Sourcing, buying, pricing, and inventory decisions</li><li>Listing quality and day-to-day marketplace administration</li><li>Returns, disputes, cases, and Resolution Center workflows</li><li>Seller-performance metrics and operational problem solving</li></ul></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Customer experience</p><h2>Trust, built repeatedly.</h2><p>Across the life of the business, Rocketeers received zero negative eBay feedback and exactly one neutral feedback. That outcome came from careful communication, clear expectations, and prompt handling when a transaction needed attention.</p></article></section>
      <section class="outcome"><p class="eyebrow">What it demonstrates</p><h2>Marketplace experience grounded in real volume and accountability.</h2><p>Rocketeers is evidence of practical judgement under operating pressure: recognizing issues early, resolving them clearly, and improving the system behind the work as volume grows.</p></section>
